# AWS Schema Conversion Tool User Guide

> Use the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (AWS SCT) to help convert a database schema to a schema you can use with AWS resources. For example, you can use AWS SCT to convert a database schema to migrate a data store to Amazon Relational Database Service (RDS), an Amazon Redshift cluster, an Amazon Aurora DB cluster, or as data stored on Amazon S3.

- [What is AWS SCT](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_Welcome.md)
- [Getting started](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_GettingStarted.md)
- [Integrating with AWS DMS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_DMSIntegration.md)
- [Migrating from a data warehouse](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/agents.md)
- [Extension packs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_ExtensionPack.md)
- [Best practices](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_BestPractices.md)
- [Troubleshooting](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_Troubleshooting.md)
- [CLI Reference](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_Reference.md)
- [Release notes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_ReleaseNotes.md)
