## [Converting application SQL](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_Converting.App.md)

- [SQL code](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_Converting.App.Generic.md): This section of the AWS Schema Conversion Tool user guide shows you how to convert SQL code in your applications with the AWS SCT.
- [SQL code in C# applications](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_Converting.App.Csharp.md): This section of the AWS Schema Conversion Tool user guide shows you how to convert SQL code in C# applications with the AWS SCT.
- [SQL code in C++](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_Converting.App.Cplusplus.md): This section of the AWS Schema Conversion Tool user guide shows you how to convert SQL code in C++ applications with AWS SCT.
- [SQL code in Java](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_Converting.App.Java.md): This section of the AWS Schema Conversion Tool user guide shows you how to convert QL code in Java applications to work with AWS database services with AWS SCT.
- [SQL code in Pro*C](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/SchemaConversionTool/latest/userguide/CHAP_Converting.App.ProC.md): This section of the AWS Schema Conversion Tool user guide shows you how to convert SQL code in Pro*C applications to work with AWS database services using AWS SCT.


